From 4079aaab16ae93ccb13554e1f572a854da0d1d36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:51:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pull the tab sheet out by dragging the address bar.

With the sheet as the tabs style, a vertical drag that starts on the
address bar and moves away from it (up from a bottom bar, down from a top
bar) opens the sheet under the finger. Letting go uses the sheet's snap
and fling rules, so it settles at half, full or closed.

This wraps the toolbar's existing swipe handler instead of adding another
touch listener. SwipeGestureListener already locks the direction once, so
a sideways drag stays the tab switching swipe and a vertical one never
switches tabs. Taps and long presses are not swipes and are unchanged.
Drags toward the bar, and every drag with the side drawer, go to the
toolbar's handler as before.

RootUiCoordinator gets a hook that returns the handler unchanged, and
TabbedRootUiCoordinator wraps it. The drawer is made the first time it is
needed, in one place, for both the button and the pull.

Tested on the Android emulator (Pixel 10 Pro profile).
